cabal-version:       3.0
name:                automata
version:             0.1.0.0
synopsis:            Two automata that are not Conway's Game of Life
description:
  Two cellular automata chosen for where they /disagree/ about what the
  library owes them.
  .
  Wireworld is four states with an asymmetric transition, and it still runs
  through the same @Stencil@ and the same @stencilGrid@ the game-of-life
  example does --- on @Clamped@ axes rather than @Periodic@ ones, which costs
  no code at all. The engine is not Life-specific.
  .
  Langton's ant is a single walker carrying a heading, which no stencil can
  express, and it runs on @Walker@ and @stepWalker@ instead. Its topology is
  a command-line flag: the same ant wraps on @Periodic@, stalls against the
  wall on @Clamped@, and bounces --- heading reversed by @transportCoord@ ---
  on @Reflective@.
license:             MIT
license-file:        LICENSE
author:              Kevin Horlick
maintainer:          beefyhalo@gmail.com
category:            Simulation
build-type:          Simple
extra-doc-files:     ChangeLog.md

executable automata
  main-is:             Main.hs
  other-modules:
    Automata.Ant
    Automata.Wireworld
  build-depends:
    , base         >=4.19 && <5
    , comonad      >=5.0  && <5.1
    , gloss        >=1.13 && <1.14
    , lens         >=5.2  && <5.4
    , grid-sized
    , vector       >=0.13 && <0.14
  hs-source-dirs:      src
  default-language:    GHC2024
  ghc-options: -O2 -threaded
    -Wall -Wcompat -Widentities -Wincomplete-record-updates
    -Wincomplete-uni-patterns -Wmissing-export-lists -Wpartial-fields
    -Wredundant-constraints -Werror
